  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (engine/COPYING.md).
  The game's pictures, sounds and levels are part of its source code, under
  the same license; there is no separate data file.
  Source: https://github.com/fragglet/sdl-sopwith, commit
  c4e034109e28a5bd1727645fe77b27430219e8b5, with frunk.store's changes for this
  site in engine/sopwith-web.patch (also tools/sopwith/sopwith-web.patch in
  https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose tools/build-sopwith.mjs
  builds it). The source the build came from is
  engine/sdl-sopwith-c4e034109e28-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: web_* functions let the page pass on touch, controllers, menu
  choices and the high score name; the game's own touch strip and its SDL
  controller support are switched off on the web, since the page provides
  both; the controller layout matches the page's, so the game's help screen
  names the same buttons; keys reach the game only while its picture has the
  focus; no "open manual" or "install as app" items in the menu.

Libraries (built in)
  Emscripten's SDL2 port, zlib license.

